ritable, configurable.\n\n- getElementAtPath: test retrieving nested.\n\n- promiseAllObject: test resolves object.\n\n- randomString: test length and characters.\n\n- esc: test JSON stringification.\n\n- isObject: test various.\n\n- isPlainObject: test plain vs custom.\n\n- numKeys: test count.\n\n- getParsedType: test various types.\n\n- escapeRegex: test escaping.\n\nWe need to import util. Some functions rely on other modules like schemas for clone, but we can skip.\n\nWrite tests using vitest.\n\nPotential issues: Node environment may not have File defined. isPlainObject uses File check? Not needed.\n\nImplement tests.\n\nEdge: allowsEval uses cached; we can test that cached works but not evaluate eval.\n\nTest for isPlainObject: plain object {} returns true; object with custom prototype returns false; maybe use Object.create(null) which has no prototype but is plain? Implementation: isObject(o) true, then ctor = o.constructor; for Object.create(null), ctor is undefined, returns true. So test that.\n\nTest for getParsedType: for array, map, set, date, promise, function, etc.\n\nImplement.\n\nLet's craft test file.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"We need to write tests for util functions covering main logic. Choose functions: getEnumValues, joinValues, jsonStringifyReplacer, cached, nullish, cleanRegex, floatSafeRemainder, defineLazy, assignProp, getElementAtPath, promiseAllObject, randomString, esc, captureStackTrace (maybe not), isObject, allowsEval (cached), isPlainObject, numKeys, getParsedType, escapeRegex, clone (maybe need schemas). But we can test simpler functions that don't require heavy dependencies.\n\nWe can import util and test:\n\n- getEnumValues: given enum-like object with numeric and string values, ensure numeric keys filtered.\n\n- joinValues: array of primitives returns string with separator.\n\n- jsonStringifyReplacer: ensure bigint converted to string.\n\n- cached: ensure lazy evaluation and caching works; also tha